  "query_preview": "/THURSDAY THROUGH SUNDAY/... \nThe long term forecast remains dry and seasonal. There is now much \nbetter confidence in the late week and weekend forecast, which \nfavors ridging building in across the West and a weak cutoff low \nforming over the Pacific west of Baja California. Weak troughing \nlooks to drag across the local area Friday into Saturday ahead of \nthe building ridge. Previous forecasts supported slight rain chances \nwith this trough, but this trough now looks completely dry and \nlatest NBM PoPs are 5% or less across the region. These are also the \nonly PoPs in the 7-day forecast. Plenty of time to dry out fallowing \nall the rain. Temperatures during the second half of the week will \nremain steady near to slightly below normal and then heading into \nthe weekend temperatures are likely to trend warmer as the ridging \nbuilds into the west. Most lower deserts may see high temperatures \nreturn to the low and possibly even mid 80s.",
